Package: lcos-base
Version: 0.9.4-2
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 104
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: lcos-archive-keyring (>= 0.7), lcos-branding (>= 0.9-1), eject, cifs-utils, keyutils, gvfs-backends, dialog, xfce4-screensaver, xarchiver, thunar-archive-plugin, exfatprogs, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
Replaces: base-files
Description: LCOS 0.9.4 identity, GRUB drop-in, X/boot-order system config
 os-release / issue for LCOS 0.9.4 (excalibur), lcos-write-os-release,
 and /etc/default/grub.d/lcos.cfg (BACKGROUND lcos-splash-1024x768.png,
 GFXMODE=1024x768, GFXPAYLOAD keep, CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT quiet splash
 loglevel=2).
 .
 AMD GPUs (0.9.2-2, #115/#118): no Xorg driver override. Xorg
 autoselects the AMD driver as in 0.8. The 0.9/0.9.1 modesetting snippets,
 /etc/init.d/lcos-amdgpu-ddx and /usr/lib/lcos/lcos-amdgpu-ddx are removed
 on upgrade.
 .
 insserv overrides so LightDM starts after elogind/seatd
 and /etc/init.d/plymouth no longer quits Plymouth at boot (LightDM is the
 single Plymouth quitter; the shutdown splash is kept).
 .
 Depends on the overlay keyring and branding artwork.
 0.9.1: recommends eject (#104) and cifs-utils + keyutils (#111). From
 0.9.1-3 they are Recommends, not Depends, so the Updates tool's plain
 apt-get upgrade moves 0.8 systems without holding lcos-base back.
 0.9.2-4: eject, cifs-utils, keyutils and gvfs-backends (Thunar SMB
 browsing) are Depends again; 0.9.2-5 adds dialog (debconf frontend,
 #125). Updates 0.9.2-2+ installs kept-back
 upgrades that only add packages, so upgraders receive them.
 0.9.3-1: ships /etc/apt/preferences.d/lcos-amd-backports.pref (not a
 conffile) with i386 Mesa pinned to excalibur-backports too (#129).
 0.9.3-2: Depends xfce4-screensaver (screen lock on lid close/suspend,
 #109), xarchiver + thunar-archive-plugin (archive manager, #132) and
 exfatprogs (exFAT tools, #131) so upgraders get the 0.9.3 ISO additions.
 0.9.3-3: Depends xdg-desktop-portal-gtk (pulls xdg-desktop-portal) so
 Chromium/Brave file pickers work (#135).
 0.9.4-2: the apt pin also takes firmware-realtek from excalibur-backports
 (newest rtw89 firmware for LLK lcos22 Realtek USB Wi-Fi, #138).
 Postinst re-applies identity on configure so apt upgrades overwrite
 stale 0.4 conffile text kept by noninteractive Updates.
